# AN END-OF-RUN READ RACE IN gen_ut_intg_store's OWN ASSERTION, found by a round-1 triage and fixed test-side.
#
# THE DEFECT, with both terms quoted. The test asserts that two counts are EQUAL:
#   evt_retired_count   incremented in the interface by a NON-BLOCKING assignment on the clock edge,
#                       gen_bridge_if.sv, "if (rvfi_valid) evt_retired_count <= evt_retired_count + 32'd1"
#   evt_isa_records     written by the scoreboard with a BLOCKING assignment as it processes a record,
#                       gen_rvfi_pkg.sv, "bvif.evt_isa_records = compared + folded"
# Two different mechanisms, so while a record is in flight the scoreboard is one ahead. The test read both back to
# back and required equality, which is only true when nothing is in flight.
#
# THE PROBE THAT SETTLED IT, before any fix was written. An out-of-tree root with a print at every site that moves
# evt_isa_records, carrying the order, compared, folded, the value written and the interface's own count. The result
# is uniform over ALL 31 records: every record took the main compare path, folded stayed 0, neither the fold nor the
# draft-B site fired once, and at every record the scoreboard's count equals the order while the interface's is
# exactly ONE BEHIND, from order 1 at 1 against 0 to order 31 at 31 against 30. Not one record deviates.
# THE DRAFT-B DOUBLE-COUNT WAS RULED OUT STATICALLY, not by the run: that site does "draft_b++; compared++" and the
# main site does "compared++", so a record taking both would double-count, but the draft-B branch returns before
# reaching the main one. The probe confirms it never fired here.
#
# THE FIX, test-side and the assertion unchanged. Between the export flush and the read, the test now waits while
# the two counts differ, one cycle at a time, up to QUIESCE_CYCLES; then it reads both and asserts equality exactly
# as before. THE BOUND DECIDES HOW LONG TO WAIT, NEVER WHETHER TO REPORT: a record the comparator never consumed
# never converges, so the loop exhausts the bound and the equality still fails. The bound is 20 cycles against a
# measured skew of one record and a record every few cycles, which is generous by a wide margin, and the reason it
# cannot mask a defect is written beside it.
#
# WHY NOT LOOSEN THE ASSERTION to "ahead by at most one", which was the alternative: the equality is the property
# worth having, that the comparator consumed every retired record, and a relation that tolerates a skew would also
# tolerate a genuine one-record skip. The wait costs cycles; the loosening costs the check.

